vision
======

A fork of cathrynlavery/diagram-design v2.6 (MIT), retoned for Korean-language use.
Upstream: https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design
Upstream license: MIT — see LICENSE (retained unchanged).

The 39 layout grammars, the §6 connector rules, the complexity budget and the
accessibility contract are upstream work and are unmodified. This fork changes
tokens and typography only.


What changed
------------

Palette — every role kept except two:

    accent        #eb6c36  ->  #0f766e   (light)      deep teal
                  #f08a59  ->  #14b8a6   (dark)
    accent-tint   rgba(235,108,54,0.08) -> rgba(15,118,110,0.08)
                  rgba(240,138,89,0.10) -> rgba(20,184,166,0.10)
    link          #2e5aa8  ->  #4c1d95   (light)      violet
                  #6a95d8  ->  #a78bfa   (dark)

`link` had to move. Teal sits 43 degrees from blue-slate `muted` in hue, so with
the upstream blue `link` the three mandatory arrow markers (muted / accent /
link) were 8x6px polygons separated by 1.22:1 contrast — indistinguishable at
that size. Violet restores an 88-degree gap from accent.

The new accent also fixes a contrast defect it inherited: `#eb6c36` on `#f5f5f5`
is 2.86:1, below WCAG AA, and nothing upstream checks the accent (the documented
contrast check covers `ink` and `muted` only). `#0f766e` is 5.02:1 light,
`#14b8a6` is 5.18:1 dark.

Typography — the upstream serif/sans split is collapsed to one family:

    title       Instrument Serif  ->  Pretendard, Noto Sans KR  (1.75rem/600)
    node-name   Geist             ->  Pretendard, Noto Sans KR
    callout     Instrument Serif italic -> Pretendard italic
    mono roles  Geist Mono        ->  unchanged

Instrument Serif and Geist carry no Hangul, so Korean labels fell back to system
fonts and broke the type system. Title and body now separate by size and weight
rather than by family.


Pretendard cannot be loaded as a webfont
----------------------------------------

`tools/lint-skin.py` accepts remote stylesheets from `fonts.googleapis.com` only,
and additionally bans `@import` and every non-fragment CSS `url()`. Pretendard is
not on Google Fonts, so linking it, self-hosting it, and embedding it as a data
URI are all rejected. That gate was left intact.

Consequence: Pretendard renders only where it is installed locally. `Noto Sans KR`
is the loaded fallback and is what any CI-rendered screenshot will show. Always
name both, in that order. Diagrams remain correct either way — both cover Hangul.


Known limitations of this fork
------------------------------

All 149 upstream assets were recoloured to the teal skin and rebranded, so
`--all` works and is green:

    python3 tools/lint-skin.py        --all --baseline   # 186 checked, 23 skipped
    python3 tools/verify-geometry.py  --all              # 188 checked
    python3 tools/verify-connectors.py --all             # 188 checked
    python3 tools/verify-spacing.py   --all              # 188 checked
    python3 scripts/self_check.py     <file>

23 files stay excluded from colour/font linting via `tools/lint-skin-baseline.txt`
— that exclusion is upstream's, carried over, plus the Korean derivatives of
three excluded originals.

Two checkers are new here and have no upstream counterpart:

  verify-connectors.py   an arrow-bearing segment running collinear with a node
                         border (SKILL.md §6 rule 5's most visible member)
  verify-spacing.py      node boxes sharing a border, overlapping, or closer
                         than the §7 minimum

Per-type verifiers carried over under tools/: verify-treemap, verify-slopegraph,
verify-ridgeline, verify-bubble, verify-dumbbell. `verify-ridgeline` and
`verify-bubble` had the upstream accent hardcoded and were repointed at the teal
tokens; `verify-dumbbell`'s prose rationale was corrected (accent-on-paper is
5.02:1 here, not 2.86:1) while its 3:1 rule was kept.

Upstream scripts NOT shipped, and the references that mention them say so:
verify-motion, verify-docs-sync, verify-plugin-package, verify-drawio-import,
verify-mermaid-import, and the test-verify-* suites. Motion output is unverified
here — check it by hand.

Nothing measures text. All four checkers parse attributes; none calls getBBox(),
so a label can overflow its box with every gate green. See lessons.md.


Korean
------

39 core types ship a Korean example at `assets/example-<type>-ko.html`, selectable
from the EN / KO toggle in `assets/index.html`. Korean covers the minimal-light
variant only, so the gallery disables KO when a non-light variant is selected and
vice versa.

Node names, titles and legends are Korean; mono technical values stay Latin —
ports, paths, SQL identifiers, package names and product names. That is both
normal Korean technical practice and the reason the translations produced no
overflow.

The 13 remaining gallery entries (bubble, ridgeline, slopegraph, the import and
animated demos, loop-terminal, sequence-oauth, quadrant-consultant,
high-level-vertical, datalake) are variants and demos, and are EN only.


Inherited defects — upstream, not introduced here
-------------------------------------------------

Not fixed, because this fork changes tokens and typography only. Recorded so
they are not mistaken for fork damage:

- Connector rules 3, 4 and 5 (overlapping connectors, shared attach points,
  transit behind non-endpoint boxes) have NO automated checker. `verify-geometry`
  checks label-mask overlap only. Several shipped examples violate the rules —
  `example-swimlane.html` uses diagonal `<line>` handoffs, an automatic fail
  under SKILL.md rule 1, and `it-state`, `dp-integration` and `high-level` each
  breach rule 4 or 5.
- `lint-skin.py`'s hex scanner false-positives on HTML numeric character
  references: `&#8594;` is reported as `color: #8594 is not in the style-guide
  palette`. Use literal characters, not `&#NNNN;` entities.
- SKILL.md's own SVG snippets use `font-size="7"` and `font-size="9"`, off the
  4px grid its §7 mandates. The style guide's per-role sizes (7-9px) are the
  intended reading; §7's size list is not exhaustive for mono roles.
- `type-swimlane.md` carries no layout grammar — no lane height, actor-column
  width, or routing rule for the reject/return edge. Derive from §6/§7.
- SKILL.md §6 mandates quarter-arc `r=8` corners; the formula it points at in
  `type-architecture.md` uses quadratic `Q` corners instead.
